  "main_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's start by understanding what the user needs. Isabella wants to check her gift card balance, confirm which credit card was used for her recent order, and possibly apply the gift card to that order or switch the payment method to her Visa. \n\nFirst, I need to authenticate her. The policy says to use email first. Her email is provided: isabella.lopez3271@example.com. So I should call find_user_id_by_email with that email. If that doesn't work, maybe use name and zip, but the email is given, so start there.\n\nOnce authenticated, get her user details to see her payment methods and gift card balance. Then check the recent order's payment method. If the order used a credit card, she might want to change it to Visa or apply the gift card. \n\nBut applying the gift card to an existing order isn't a standard action. The policy allows modifying payment methods for pending orders. If the order is pending, she can change the payment method. If it's already processed or delivered, that's not possible. So I need to check the order status first. \n\nWait, she mentioned \"recent order,\" but didn't provide the order ID. So I need to get her user details to list her orders and find the most recent one. Then check its status. If it's pending, maybe modify payment. If not, explain that it's too late. \n\nAlso, applying the gift card balance would require checking if the gift card has enough funds. But the tools don't have a direct function to check gift card balance; it's part of the user details. So after getting user details, I can see the gift card balance there. \n\nSo the steps are: authenticate via email, get user details, find recent order, check its status and payment method, then determine possible actions. \n\nFirst tool call: find_user_id_by_email with the provided email. Then proceed from there.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"find_user_id_by_email\", \"arguments\": {\"email\": \"isabella.lopez3271@example.com\"}}\n",
